{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the congregation gathered, etc.</b> This is one of the places where a little holds the much (Bereshit Rabbah 5)." "<b>Shall we bring forth water from this rock?</b> Because they did not recognize it — for when the well was withdrawn, that rock went and settled among the other rocks, and Israel would say to them: Why, from which rock would you bring forth water for us? Therefore he said to them: <b>Hear now, ye rebels</b> — rebellious ones, a Greek term for obstinate, defying their defiers — shall we bring forth water for you from this rock, concerning which we were not commanded?"], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:42.498115072Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}